    "comparison": "Normal and stronger variants agree on every retained non-visual indexed component after resolving local references to hierarchy/script identities. Four original prefab-bound clock sources and the full projectile/template closure are retained; this comparison alone grants no support.",
    "channel": "Uses the shared source-backed ChargeRift controller: initial5s readiness, canonical15s channel hold, speed10 flight to a live non-full Leak Marker then1s SP pulses, current target retained beyond initial range, DEF contribution2 while affecting, and10s cooldown after channel end. Accepted forced silence interrupts the silenceable link, including short accepted applications. Default canonical silence immunity still applies. Brief action controls, hidden/removed owner, source-life replacement, marker retirement/cycle rollover and battle end retire unborn SP output and clear movement/DEF holds. Callback invalidation is rechecked after each marker gain.",
    "attack": "Source ordinary Attack emits a speed10, ten-second homing Arts projectile at its existing shared attack clock. It does not stop solely for owner death. Current same-life ATK and modifiers are read on impact; after owner-object reuse it uses a captured birth-deployment source view rather than a replacement deployment. Target lives remain projectile-system owned.",
    "carrier": "One non-silenceable ON_OWNER_KILLED summon attempt per deployment, using DeadSummon.max_cnt1. The original named range x-4 contains all nine offsets of the3x3 neighborhood, including diagonals and center. Existing shared placement excludes unavailable, occupied, high, blocked, unbuildable and already occupied-by-source tiles. A failed placement makes no synthetic body and duplicate death dispatch cannot retry. Leak, removal, replacement and battle end cannot emit a summon.",
    "limits": "Native numeric callback/FSM ordering, channel travel/repeat cadence, marker selection/placement ties and retirement source views retain explicit shared-engine mappings. Native compiled/frame parity and visual work remain held."
